{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793692175,"nonce":"aVJaEb1TO3Ze1802u9eduuHV498=","title":"Language benchmark pages show each machine's recent average against PyPy and LuaJIT","message":"A tab shows one run of one machine, so the pages gave no single figure per machine, and the machine mix changes from run to run. Each page now has a table below the results with one row per machine and one column: the geometric mean, over the machine's last five runs, of how much faster zypy is than PyPy (zylua than LuaJIT) across the benchmarks, plus an All machines row counting those runs once each. It follows the Benchmark time / Full process switch. Only the last five runs count because the code changes between runs (the user asked for this window).\n\ncarry_machines.py stores one summary line per run in machines/history.json (rows counted, warm and cold geometric-mean speedup, rows won), carried forward at every deploy; it keeps every run and the page takes the last five per machine. The first deploy starts from .github/scripts/history-seed/, built from the result artifacts of the 14 runs from 2026-10-31 to 2026-11-02 (27 runs per suite), because the published site had no history.\n\nRead with the win count above the main table: a geometric mean lets a few large wins outweigh many small losses. On the seeded history zylua averages faster than LuaJIT by benchmark time and slower by full process time on every machine seen.\n\nUnverified in CI until the first deploy after the push.","files":null}]}